; claude: a small Emacs Lisp (languages/README.md): Lisp (the
; values, and printing them), Lisp_read (the reader, over sexpr/'s),
; Lisp_eval (eval
; and apply, dynamic scope, the state threaded as a value; a host adds
; its functions and special forms), Lisp_prelude (the macros written
; in Lisp: when, dolist...). TinyEmacs (apps/devtools/) is its host:
; appkits/editor's Emacs_editor gives it a buffer to change.
;
; Pure OCaml, no Playground. In the package tiny_languages, as
; tiny_languages.lisp.
(library
 (name lisp)
 (public_name tiny_languages.lisp)
 (wrapped false)
 (libraries sexpr) ; Lisp_read's reading, the syntax shared with Scheme
)
